      "content": "Dear Editor,\n\nI am submitting a pre-review of the manuscript titled \"Quantum Decoherence in Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum Devices: An Error Correction Protocol\" for consideration in Nature Physics.\n\nAfter a meticulous analysis of your study, I have identified critical concerns that could mar the scientific integrity and potential impacts of your findings. I would like to detail these issues under several pertinent headings for your consideration and their further elucidation.\n\n1. Understanding of Source of Noise in NISQ: Your assumption of noise sources in NISQ devices should be extensively revised. In the discussion section of the paper, your review of quantum decoherence barely touches upon various intricacies of NISQ environments, thereby not explicitly addressing the issue of crosstalk between qubits during gate operations. Crosstalk could significantly skew the data pertaining to success rates, giving an impression of higher quantum fidelity than possibly achieved. I encourage the incorporation of comprehensive depictions pertaining to crosstalk as a crucial determinant of noise in NISQ devices.\n\n2. Error Mitigation Protocols: Regarding methodologies, the range of error mitigation protocols warrant more robust treatment. While your manuscript debates error correction, it does not provide an in-depth exploration or comparison of various techniques such as randomized benchmarking",
